  "cwe": [
   {
    "value": "CWE-377",
    "origin": "cna",
    "description": "CWE-377 Insecure Temporary File"
   }
  ],
  "desc": "Insecure Temporary File vulnerability in Mix deps.partition in Elixir allows a local user to execute code as another user via a swapped partition config file. Partitioned dependency compilation passes the project configuration to each partition VM through a file in a fixed-name directory under the shared system temporary directory, and the partition trusts what it reads back. Another local user on the same host can exploit this during a mix deps.compile run that uses partitioned compilation.\n\nMix.Tasks.Deps.Partition.server/4 in lib/mix/lib/mix/tasks/deps.partition.ex creates the directory with File.mkdir_p/1, which accepts an existing directory without checking its owner, so a user who created it first can replace the file before client/0 reads it.\n\nThis issue affects mix: from 1.20.0-rc.4 before 1.20.5.",
