tional generalization across mathematical reasoning, coding, agent, and long-context capabilities using Qwen3 models. Across extrapolative settings, OPD and MOPD reach 96.04-102.73% of their teachers' IND scores. Yet their out-of-distribution (OOD) scores remain 2.45-16.25% below the base model's. Across three compositional settings, MOPD improves IND performance over the base model, but its performance on composed tasks as OOD remains 18.19-24.34% below that of the best teachers. To understand these gaps, we examine teacher capability and data coverage as two potential bottlenecks. Jointly alleviating these bottlenecks eliminates OOD forgetting in our experiments and suggests the potential for generalization beyond the teacher. (M)OPD also reduces OOD forgetting on average relative to its reinforcement learning (RL) baselines. Analysis of the associated update geometry reveals smaller and more spectrally concentrated updates on average than those of the RL baselines, along with greater shared update structure under MOPD. Motivated by these findings, we propose geometry-based patching and base-preserving replay to improve OOD performance while largely preserving IND performance. Our findings identify a blind spot in capability consolidation via (M)OPD, highlighting the need for algorithms that explicitly support OOD retention and generalization.\",\"upvotes\":3,\"discussionId\":\"6aec1df3870269964d13ad91\",\"projectPage\":\"https://yichenzw.com/opd-generalization.github.io/\",\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"653b817d32c97d0655575872\",\"name\":\"ByteDance\",\"fullname\":\"ByteDance\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6535c9e88bde2fae19b6fb25/0clr54wj5Ly-RkYU9OXPp.png\"}},\"canReadDatabase\":false,\"canManagePapers\":false,\"canSubmit\":false,\"hasHfLevelAccess\":false,\"upvoted\":false,\"upvoters\":[{\"_id\":\"6484fe4e22e3c63f5ec0a23a\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6484fe4e22e3c63f5ec0a23a/roXzheKehiq2m60b_gXwX.png\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Yichen Zach Wang\",\"user\":\"ZachW\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6aec455b21ea458819a12953\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/FBFYwRFqWFPmE8gblFS6D.png\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"minjun kim\",\"user\":\"minjunkimmm\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6a2da6c8ca070ee12c6e396c\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/d5adda946bf33aa6c75a4da067cc8f69.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Joe Mama\",\"user\":\"JoeMama123123123\",\"type\":\"user\"}],\"acceptLanguages\":[\"*\"],\"dailyPaperRank\":0,\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"653b817d32c97d0655575872\",\"name\":\"ByteDance\",\"fullname\":\"ByteDance\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6535c9e88bde2fae19b6fb25/0clr54wj5Ly-RkYU9OXPp.png\"},\"query\":{}}\"> Papers arxiv:2611.05609 On the Generalization Limitation of On-Policy Distillation for Post-RL Consolidation Published on Nov 3 · Submitted by Yichen Zach Wang on Nov 5 · ByteDance Upvote 3 Authors: Yichen Wang , Yufa Zhou , Siqi Zhu , Haozheng Luo , Jingzhi Bao , Zhichao Liu , Zijun Wei Abstract M u l t i - t e a c h e r o n - p o l i c y d i s t i l l a t i o n ( M O P D ) e x t e n d s o n - p o l i c y d i s t i l l a t i o n ( O P D ) t o c o n s o l i d a t e c a p a b i l i t i e s f r o m m u l t i p l e t e a c h e r s . A l t h o u g h p r i o r w o r k r e p o r t s n e a r - p e r f e c t i n - d i s t r i b u t i o n ( I N D ) d i s t i l l a t i o n p e r f o r m a n c e , w e f i n d t h a t t h i s c a n m a s k i n c o m p l e t e c a p a b i l i t y c o n s o l i d a t i o n b e y o n d t h e s u p e r v i s e d d i s t r i b u t i o n . A p r e l i m i n a r y s t u d y o n s y n t h e t i c r e a s o n i n g s h o w s t h a t O P D d o e s n o t f u l l y t r a n s f e r t e a c h e r s ' g e n e r a l i z a t i o n c a p a b i l i t i e s . W e t h e n e x t e n d t h i s i n v e s t i g a t i o n t o r e a l - w o r l d t a s k s , e v a l u a t i n g e x t r a p o l a t i v e a n d c o m p o s i t i o n a l g e n e r a l i z a t i o n a c r o s s m a t h e m a t i c a l r e a s o n i n g , c o d i n g , a g e n t , a n d l o n g - c o n t e x t c a p a b i l i t i e s u s i n g Q w e n 3 m o d e l s . A c r o s s e x t r a p o l a t i v e s e t t i n g s , O P D a n d M O P D r e a c h 9 6 . 0 4 - 1 0 2 . 7 3 % o f t h e i r t e a c h e r s ' I N D s c o r e s . Y e t t h e i r o u t - o f - d i s t r i b u t i o n ( O O D ) s c o r e s r e m a i n 2 . 4 5 - 1 6 . 2 5 % b e l o w t h e b a s e m o d e l ' s . A c r o s s t h r e e c o m p o s i t i o n a l s e t t i n g s , M O P D i m p r o v e s I N D p e r f o r m a n c e o v e r t h e b a s e m o d e l , b u t i t s p e r f o r m a n c e o n c o m p o s e d t a s k s a s O O D r e m a i n s 1 8 . 1 9 - 2 4 . 3 4 % b e l o w t h a t o f t h e b e s t t e a c h e r s . T o u n d e r s t a n d t h e s e g a p s , w e e x a m i n e t e a c h e r c a p a b i l i t y a n d d a t a c o v e r a g e a s t w o p o t e n t i a l b o t t l e n e c k s . J o i n t l y a l l e v i a t i n g t h e s e b o t t l e n e c k s e l i m i n a t e s O O D f o r g e t t i n g i n o u r e x p e r i m e n t s a n d s u g g e s t s t h e p o t e n t i a l f o r g e n e r a l i z a t i o n b e y o n d t h e t e a c h e r . ( M ) O P D a l s o r e d u c e s O O D f o r g e t t i n g o n a v e r a g e r e l a t i v e t o i t s r e i n f o r c e m e n t l e a r n i n g ( R L ) b a s e l i n e s . A n a l y s i s o f t h e a s s o c i a t e d u p d a t e g e o m e t r y r e v e a l s s m a l l e r a n d m o r e s p e c t r a l l y c o n c e n t r a t e d u p d a t e s o n a v e r a g e t h a n t h o s e o f t h e R L b a s e l i n e s , a l o n g w i t h g r e a t e r s h a r e d u p d a t e s t r u c t u r e u n d e r M O P D . M o t i v a t e d b y t h e s e f i n d i n g s , w e p r o p o s e g e o m e t r y - b a s e d p a t c h i n g a n d b a s e - p r e s e r v i n g r e p l a y t o i m p r o v e O O D p e r f o r m a n c e w h i l e l a r g e l y p r e s e r v i n g I N D p e r f o r m a n c e . O u r f i n d i n g s i d e n t i f y a b l i n d s p o t i n c a p a b i l i t y c o n s o l i d a t i o n v i a ( M ) O P D , h i g h l i g h t i n g t h e n e e d f o r a l g o r i t h m s t h a t e x p l i c i t l y s u p p o r t O O D r e t e n t i o n a n d g e n e r a l i z a t i o n . View arXiv page View PDF Project page Add to collection Community ZachW Paper submitter about 7 hours ago • edited about 6 hours ago Hi everyone! I’m the first author of this paper. \n We identify a blind spot in (M)OPD for post-RL consolidation: students may not inherit their teachers’ generalization capabilities, even when they achieve near-perfect in-distribution distillation performance. \n We investigate this on a large scale, across math, coding, agent, and long-context tasks, using different student and teacher models. \n We also analyze and explore preliminary patching methods. We’d love to discuss more about how to further improve generalization in (M)OPD! \n Project page: https://yichenzw.com/opd-generalization.github.io/ \n Huge thanks to all my co-authors for their contributions to this project! \n See translation Reply orinmemory about 4 hours ago Great to see OOD retention measured separately from IND distillation quality; \"near-perfect IND can mask incomplete consolidation\" is something many people assume but rarely quantify. For me the most practical result is base-preserving replay: adding coding prompts supervised by the base model lifts AIME25 avg@8 to 67.50 for the GSM8K OPD student, with only a 0.18-point drop on GSM8K. Did you look at how the replay ratio trades off against IND performance, and whether replay and Procrustes-attention patching stack? \n See translation Reply Edit Preview Upload images, audio, and videos by dragging in the text input, pasting, or clicking here . Tap or paste here to upload images Comment · Sign up or log in to comment Upvote 3 Models citing this paper 0 No model linking this paper Cite arxiv.org/abs/2611.05609 in a model README.md to link it from this page. Datasets citing this paper 0 No dataset linking this paper Cite arxiv.org/abs/2611.05609 in a dataset README.md to link it from this page. Spaces citing this paper 0 No Space linking this paper Cite arxiv.org/abs/2611.05609 in a Space README.md to link it from this page. Collections including this paper 0 No Collection including this paper Add this paper to a collection to link it from this page. System theme Company TOS Privacy About Careers Website Models Datasets Spaces Pricing Docs \n \n \n \n \n \n"
